# ChainOpt project rules

## What this is
ChainOpt analyzes LLM pipelines and surfaces evidence-backed recommendations for reducing cost and latency. Python SDK + CLI, FastAPI analysis service, Supabase Postgres with pgvector, Next.js dashboard.

## Authoritative spec
The technical spec is docs/SPEC.md. When a task prompt says "per Section N" or "per the masterplan", it means docs/SPEC.md. Read the referenced section before writing code. Do not modify docs/SPEC.md unless a task explicitly says to.

## Repo boundaries
apps/landing/ is the existing marketing site. Never modify, move, refactor, or reference it. It is out of scope for every task.

## Non-negotiables
- Never invent model names, model IDs, or pricing. All of that lives in packages/chainopt/src/chainopt/registry/models.json, which is human-maintained. Read it; never write it. If a model is missing, fail loudly rather than guessing.
- Never fabricate savings numbers, benchmark results, or test output. If you did not run it, say you did not run it.
- The SDK must never raise into user code. Every chainopt code path inside the interception layer is wrapped in try/except and degrades to silence.
- Every task ends with tests that actually run. Paste real command output. Do not write "tests pass" without the output.
- No new dependencies without stating why in the response.

## Naming contracts
CallRecord, CallSiteRef, IngestBatch, PipelineGraph, FindingCandidate and their field names are fixed contracts across the SDK, API, and dashboard. Do not rename or "improve" them.

## Style
- Python 3.10+, ruff, line length 100, full type annotations on public functions, pydantic v2 for all boundary data.
- Prefer explicit over clever. This code will be read by prospective customers auditing what it collects.
- No emoji in code, logs, or CLI output.
- Errors tell the user what to do next, not just what went wrong.

## Testing
- pytest, respx for httpx mocking, real Postgres for API tests.
- Every flag detector gets synthetic fixtures with both positive and NEGATIVE cases. A detector without a negative test is not done.
- Any external API (Anthropic, OpenAI) is injected behind an interface so tests never hit the network.

## Cost discipline
Static analysis must prefilter deterministically before any LLM call. One LLM request per file, cached by content hash. One adjudication request per flag type per run. If a change would increase LLM calls, say so explicitly.
